# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy this file to .env and fill in what you want to use.
# Every variable is OPTIONAL. With an empty .env, all 12 skills still work:
# they draft, and you copy-paste into LinkedIn. Nothing breaks.
#
#   cp .env.example .env       (macOS / Linux)
#   copy .env.example .env     (Windows)
#
# Then run:  python bin/lk.py doctor
# It reports exactly which integrations are live and what degrades without each.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── 1. DeepSeek ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Only needed for `lk draft`, the outside-the-chat drafting path.
# Drafting inside the chat needs NO key: the agent is the model.
# Get one: https://platform.deepseek.com/api_keys
DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=
# Optional overrides:
# DEEPSEEK_MODEL=deepseek-chat          # or deepseek-reasoner
# DEEPSEEK_API_BASE=https://api.deepseek.com

# ── 2. Publora ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This is the layer that POSTS to LinkedIn on your approval. It is also the only
# way this bundle publishes without you copy-pasting, because LinkedIn has no
# public API for third-party posting without a partner integration.
#
# You never hand over your LinkedIn password. You authorize LinkedIn *inside
# Publora's dashboard*, and Publora holds the token. This bundle only ever sees
# a Publora API key.
#
#   1. Sign up free:  https://app.publora.com/signup   (15 posts/month free)
#   2. Channels -> Add Channel -> LinkedIn -> authorize
#   3. Click your LinkedIn channel and copy the ID, e.g. linkedin-ABC123DEF
#   4. Settings (gear, bottom-left) -> API -> Create Key, copy the sk_... string
#
# Free tier covers 15 posts a month, which is more than a daily-posting habit
# needs if you also use the draft-only path for some of them.
PUBLORA_API_KEY=
LINKEDIN_PLATFORM_ID=

# If you leave LINKEDIN_PLATFORM_ID empty, the engine tries to derive it from
# the key. That works when your account has exactly one LinkedIn channel, and
# refuses when it has several - picking one for you could publish to the wrong
# account, so it asks instead.

# ── 3. Apify (the READ side) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Lets the reading skills fetch a post body, its comment thread, your own recent
# comments, and the people who liked or commented - by URL, with no cookies and
# no LinkedIn login.
#
# Without it, those skills ask you to paste the text instead. Everything still
# works; it is just one more paste.
#
#   Sign up: https://console.apify.com/sign-up   ($5/month free credit)
#   Token:   https://console.apify.com/settings/integrations
#
# At roughly $1-$5 per 1,000 results, daily comment work stays well under $2/month.
APIFY_TOKEN=

# ── 4. Pixfaro (illustrations) ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Generates a feed image, a carousel slide, or a quote-card of your hook, and
# composites your handle or logo on it as a pixel-exact overlay. Returns a hosted
# URL that flows straight into the publish step.
#
# Without it, the skills draft the image prompt and you generate it yourself.
#
#   Sign up: https://api.pixfaro.com/signup   (key format: pf_live_...)
#   Verify:  python vendor/scripts/check_config.py
PIXFARO_TOKEN=

# ── 5. Advanced: your own publisher (Tier 2) ─────────────────────────────────
# If you have built your own posting script, point the bundle at it. It receives
# the payload as JSON on stdin and the kind/target as argv.
#
# Caution: this executes whatever it points at, on approval. Set it only to
# something you wrote and understand. A draft can never set this variable.
# LINKEDIN_SKILLS_CUSTOM_POSTER=python /path/to/my-poster.py
